        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(mcp): open App views from channel replies",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nMCP App tool results already render inline in Control UI, but channel turns lose that interactive view. Telegram, Slack, Discord, and text-only transports preserve the assistant text yet provide no way to open the latest successful App view.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis carries only the latest successful view identity through the agent result, then materializes one portable `web-app` presentation action after the final visible reply has been normalized. The Gateway mints the existing standalone-view ticket at that last moment, bounds it to the live view lease, and uses one lifecycle-owned HTTPS origin prepared by Tailscale Serve or Funnel. Channel adapters retain transport ownership; prerequisite #111116 keeps Telegram's native `web_app` button DM-only and falls back to the portable HTTPS action elsewhere.\n\nControl UI remains unchanged and receives no duplicate action. Missing origin, capacity, lease, transport support, or an expired view leaves the original reply text intact. The action contains only a fixed label and opaque URL; App HTML, input/result data, session identity, view metadata, and bearer credentials are not serialized into channel payloads.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can open the latest MCP App from the final assistant reply in Telegram DMs, Slack, and Discord. Other transports keep an understandable text-and-link fallback. Tailscale Serve links remain tailnet-only; Funnel links are internet-reachable. Existing reply text and Control UI behavior are preserved.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- 392 exact-head agent, Gateway, Telegram, Slack, and Discord tests passed on `42cddb7ebd58cad73b9e685e605f1e4ce90b224a` before the known first-navigation browser cold start: [run 29674084298](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29674084298).\n- Exact-head browser conformance then passed twice consecutively after that reproducible cold-start retry, followed by a clean full dead-code scan: [run 29674158631](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29674158631).\n- Full changed gate, private-QA build, and canonical package tarball integrity passed on Blacksmith Testbox: [run 29672729609](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29672729609).\n- Exact-head GitHub CI is tracked at [run 29674267906](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29674267906).\n- Fresh whole-branch autoreview after the final rebase and accepted channel-less guard reported no actionable findings (0.90 confidence).\n- The credentialed exact-head Telegram Desktop/Mini App Crabbox workflow failed closed with a blocker manifest: [run 29674274494](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29674274494). The current capture flow cannot inject the MCP App fixture or publish a Gateway Serve/Funnel origin, so native button receipt/open, app-only tool invocation, resource read, and expired state remain unproven. This PR must not merge until that real-user proof is available.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I understand and reviewed the full owner/caller/callee/channel surface and addressed the accepted autoreview finding before opening this PR.\n",
